The rest of Go's standard library on Radix (ADR 0350): the C library's
ways that macOS and OpenBSD take (the *at functions, writev, accept4,
pipe2, getrandom) with Linux's structures (stat, dirent, socket
options); time zones from /system/resources/zoneinfo and root
certificates from /system/resources/certificates; the host name from
uname; the program's path from the runtime. Until Radix's event queue and
networking, net lists no interfaces and has neither sendfile nor splice.
Dukovo only.

